M=100
N=$((M * 10))
/usr/bin/time ./show_addr ${S} ${M} ${N}
<!--- end code --->

## Julia

* In Julia, to print an address of an array `b`, you first get a pointer by `p = pointer(b)` and cast it into an integer by `Int64(p)`
